fe-0a5ce320ef44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311924} {:answer/id #uuid "811a26be-6de9-512e-a7ae-42a733c69318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311925} {:answer/id #uuid "e02bfad2-bbaa-5529-9ce2-5d495cf282d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f585a8a-9b61-5618-aafe-0a5ce320ef44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311924} :answer-field/id #uuid "c29a584f-5796-56db-b609-531eeaff29f0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d49d62d-3171-54ed-829e-5b8164e0d4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311928} {:answer/id #uuid "485056da-64ab-53c7-a5e8-cb9070c020a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311929} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e4974d-1594-5af6-b2aa-0fb4f34e7faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311930} {:answer/id #uuid "491ddb23-1835-5387-becf-e8a79fdffbd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311931} {:answer/id #uuid "3495262f-ed50-5b4b-8be5-00cdb7ed6da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "485056da-64ab-53c7-a5e8-cb9070c020a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311929} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e35d80-0d12-57f7-8154-318fb39ebee5" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54e0af89-1e9b-5900-bf6e-4113ca0cfa32" :question/math-academy-id "q-335071" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2{e}^{4x}+x,$ then $f=O({e}^{4x})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{x}{2{e}^{4x}})=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,x=O(2{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(4{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O({e}^{4x})$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation.\n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each selected step.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand this follows by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx=O(2{e}^{4x}).\n$$\n\nSince $f=2{e}^{4x}+x,$ by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=2{e}^{4x}+x=O(2{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x})=O(4{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nwhich justifies line $\\text{L4}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(4{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand by $\\text{the constant multiple property}$ with $c=4,$ we conclude\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{4x}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of Big-O"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "debf6873-0622-578b-b420-859033d3d8c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311935} {:answer/id #uuid "11c54f67-458b-5dab-af5f-930a2e74c050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311936} {:answer/id #uuid "eef891e4-ad80-5e5e-a2e9-61c0b8ef6780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311937} {:answer/id #uuid "67bbbdaa-4331-54b2-b8d3-05938de37e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311938} {:answer/id #uuid "38e7bc7e-8c84-5a1f-a102-7a2653c5d831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38e7bc7e-8c84-5a1f-a102-7a2653c5d831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311939} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e8733d0-4555-50d8-84be-1528ecde2ebf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311934} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be295c8e-ee15-50ae-8630-35363677913a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311941} {:answer/id #uuid "2533c1fb-45b8-5f32-8350-d39076a8bf7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2533c1fb-45b8-5f32-8350-d39076a8bf7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311942} :answer-field/id #uuid "25237a46-70f9-5f67-a34f-27cdd7222471" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4d4f396-cca9-52a4-94a0-fad653427237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311944} {:answer/id #uuid "fdfa317e-327c-5ddf-8b13-6089e559bec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311945} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7e4782-6f5b-5cf1-b030-87f198f97ae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311946} {:answer/id #uuid "f1056c69-629a-5942-8843-952c62c5d786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311947} {:answer/id #uuid "16843b30-e7c5-501c-bd28-efb0912b6a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e7e4782-6f5b-5cf1-b030-87f198f97ae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311946} :answer-field/id #uuid "961bd406-1d16-550b-a5cb-3b0e1b1efbc2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad8b8afa-1813-52c9-afa7-e0b5044cbe40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311950} {:answer/id #uuid "20585ad2-529a-535e-861a-245a9674c2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311951} {:answer/id #uuid "2d1d8fc0-3304-546d-8930-10ef6b3b685b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20585ad2-529a-535e-861a-245a9674c2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311951} :answer-field/id #uuid "9183d02c-3ef4-50d5-9fbf-134f09febdb2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311949} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a388b3-c4fc-532a-91a3-4be71fef9fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311954} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4dbf0c-56d6-5bc5-bb73-8eb865b99c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311955} {:answer/id #uuid "1bbc9c42-b35b-5fa7-b85a-673a5dcb658a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311956} {:answer/id #uuid "5884a82c-a8b8-5947-b5ac-77cb84e1a06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive  property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311957} {:answer/id #uuid "4a194d04-8fa6-5aaf-90e3-63863ac6ba09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a4dbf0c-56d6-5bc5-bb73-8eb865b99c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311955} :answer-field/id #uuid "40da6823-2044-5d69-984f-0bb0b1ab4756" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e15b51c9-b3ac-5fdf-bdd1-db7479e393a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335438" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ then $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,3x=O(3x)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2x})=1$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(5x)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n3x=O({{3x}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n3x=O(3x),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L4}$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=5,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of Big-O"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89291100-6cb8-50d9-8f62-17b9f1b58a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311961} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7e38c5-acc1-5550-977f-42360d578493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311962} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb23a7f-4de9-5c6c-9d41-dd4adc5eb57e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311963} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb4e8e0-0c0b-5454-93cc-4de46b2dcb8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311964} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5289a1-5839-572a-a644-3647f407222a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe5289a1-5839-572a-a644-3647f407222a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311965} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbde3753-4a39-5de6-881c-d25082251a4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4fdba7-4688-50ae-bb8b-b4963aaf5d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2 and L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311967} {:answer/id #uuid "141d647b-c8ca-5e01-99c0-ed2b01a8bfe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1 and L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "141d647b-c8ca-5e01-99c0-ed2b01a8bfe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1 and L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311968} :answer-field/id #uuid "6457f3e6-da4b-5b4d-93e2-49caf7c98acd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9cf3ff-409f-5ec1-bff5-b4104162f53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311970} {:answer/id #uuid "5222dc4f-05e3-554b-ad87-a1b35ac97426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311971} {:answer/id #uuid "f640b32c-1ece-5f13-be57-d97ca376e254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311972} {:answer/id #uuid "7251a883-36b4-55fa-b9d0-b641ab780515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311973} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbfca92-dd6a-5cae-860b-39c8163afd64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c9cf3ff-409f-5ec1-bff5-b4104162f53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311970} :answer-field/id #uuid "359a90f1-560c-581b-a4bf-c6960fd5fd46" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edcca080-8fde-5a68-a475-177d3ccbcb6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311976} {:answer/id #uuid "57e1d75c-ed1c-5f1f-8b06-f74f690c6008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311977} {:answer/id #uuid "522b77b0-05d5-54c4-a0fc-105385ee30cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edcca080-8fde-5a68-a475-177d3ccbcb6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311976} :answer-field/id #uuid "99cbf787-e718-59fb-b2ab-4df5f7a11a16" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab1fde28-e6af-5704-8174-7dad9e9db494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311980} {:answer/id #uuid "6aec5de7-f312-5a91-bf12-3c37369d945d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311981} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f376e8-38b1-5b8a-a981-de385508e306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311982} {:answer/id #uuid "26edda93-794e-5bc2-ba59-ad3bb12fc036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311983} {:answer/id #uuid "16b57961-32f5-5cd4-8c94-878c63c6c7b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aec5de7-f312-5a91-bf12-3c37369d945d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311981} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e512a2-f362-576f-8e70-f593d950f9c8" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac4293b7-4265-5467-bc7b-b86d5611daed" :question/math-academy-id "q-335445" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2+{e}^{-x},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(2+{e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,{e}^{-x}=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{2+{e}^{-x}}_{⏟}}_{f}),\n$$\n\nand this is true by the $\\text{reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2+{e}^{-x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x}=O(2).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines   $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and the  $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(2).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2)\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of Big-O"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9080b2de-975c-5841-b631-d40d97ed4671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311987} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a5cff2-d42b-5013-9907-c6996d0c2163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311988} {:answer/id #uuid "15aaf69d-a4e3-542b-a22e-8dffb4e1daea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311989} {:answer/id #uuid "0a178694-5719-5f4e-8835-a0fd1ade120b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311990} {:answer/id #uuid "8b19563e-d9d5-5a51-afd0-f90d122b1275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b19563e-d9d5-5a51-afd0-f90d122b1275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311991} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b5fbd66-8af9-5f84-86c7-a1de13121f77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311986} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c491a06-5d14-5c81-892d-9e9490e64a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311993} {:answer/id #uuid "cee3f4bc-95bb-5502-bc0d-9ea8b0b27476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c491a06-5d14-5c81-892d-9e9490e64a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311993} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5cba3d8-f257-5ed4-b08d-4d9e2e560052" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddf408a4-455d-52b0-941f-75508718e923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311996} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a4b59b-6bed-5b29-be64-8b44087e6242" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311997} {:answer/id #uuid "66546ff6-144f-5c16-9993-efd709b1b806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311998} {:answer/id #uuid "3000ed66-22ba-56de-9aac-8fb6f12c2fa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311999} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0877ad-7fc7-5acd-836f-643432372ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddf408a4-455d-52b0-941f-75508718e923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311996} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c1fdfbc-37cb-5673-a689-af46721e9f79" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97811403-d762-5a70-9429-bf3afbcc805d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3 and L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312002} {:answer/id #uuid "adfa8169-c6e1-5c45-a246-17dbe1df7363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1 and L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97811403-d762-5a70-9429-bf3afbcc805d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3 and L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312002} :answer-field/id #uuid "88010da3-44bf-5b07-a954-5fbf0a9187ad" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58b0f60b-882e-5423-a424-390495fede9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312005} {:answer/id #uuid "e3190c99-1383-5429-9a2e-efa74630d605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312006} {:answer/id #uuid "25a90e73-ba40-5171-b649-ec678c10c388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312007} {:answer/id #uuid "03ee732f-20f2-5db7-8a0f-b9eb8c8409fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312008} {:answer/id #uuid "def4822e-f24d-5b86-9042-4e2ae46ca1ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03ee732f-20f2-5db7-8a0f-b9eb8c8409fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312008} :answer-field/id #uuid "8616f32e-13e5-5b41-8f2a-6935ae4918c7" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bd29f25-c33e-50d6-8d78-85c77962431d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335462" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x})$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,f=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,\\frac{1}{x}=O(1)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}),\n$$\n\nand this is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1})\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}=O(1).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines   $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and $\\text{the transitive property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of Big-O"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec20a16e-cb9d-5ed4-9555-a01382ef72b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312012} {:answer/id #uuid "4bed3df3-fa77-5623-8043-c836c3d66d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312013} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c06dfb-d9e7-5e16-b9ba-b26c1d7106df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312014} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2deb81-01a0-5735-891c-6c74ae771cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312015} {:answer/id #uuid "8417336b-1fd9-533b-b517-faf09c3bf4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8417336b-1fd9-533b-b517-faf09c3bf4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312016} :answer-field/id #uuid "d895d4d9-0863-5766-bef7-80ae0f3ddd00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac5e610-bf77-5460-b6d8-ee4e65ef30bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312018} {:answer/id #uuid "8773d094-8ba6-536f-8cea-36b8b66671e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8773d094-8ba6-536f-8cea-36b8b66671e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312019} :answer-field/id #uuid "6091ca3f-cde9-5614-949c-e1aa88fd1f23" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3728d1a-cae2-57ab-9be5-91ce3bdecd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312021} {:answer/id #uuid "fc39d8a1-df57-5d8d-9ea5-d1903bc7b120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312022} {:answer/id #uuid "06109531-b2d4-56fd-8e84-cd8f5241ea3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312023} {:answer/id #uuid "ac7ea0c5-ab32-5ca1-9d1a-aa76ee0553d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312024} {:answer/id #uuid "fa909451-acb8-58ad-b710-fd08aacd9789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3728d1a-cae2-57ab-9be5-91ce3bdecd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312021} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab1d23f-0c61-526e-91ed-01d0ec7266e1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aabce835-08a6-56a8-b0f2-22d9384b0c2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312027} {:answer/id #uuid "e489cee6-ef3e-5c3b-9f23-e15b3f9fb26f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312028} {:answer/id #uuid "84d04d3f-0aa5-5192-b892-ae9c470ec6f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aabce835-08a6-56a8-b0f2-22d9384b0c2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312027} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7a2c3a4-8f21-5f68-b437-c71247310fe4" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232b2854-bc6f-5c19-b90a-f11da1903761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312031} {:answer/id #uuid "06004eb1-d6ed-5f92-804c-1bc954b8fd62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312032} {:answer/id #uuid "9726151e-714b-5a56-8624-2cc1f3c0a4a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312033} {:answer/id #uuid "654fb9e5-f871-5ba7-b444-e894d7aed45b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312034} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8b9622-d29a-5e20-853b-104361febf53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06004eb1-d6ed-5f92-804c-1bc954b8fd62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312032} :answer-field/id #uuid "38e7a7e1-04c5-5a86-9ba8-e8743de99f2c" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f486a0b-746a-5894-968d-0df3eeeabb50" :question/math-academy-id "q-335474" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-x+5,$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(4{x}^{2}-x+5)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{4{x}^{2}-x}{5})=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,4{x}^{2}-x=O(5)$  as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(5)$  as $x\\to 0$   \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  as $x\\to 0$ \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation.\n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each selected step.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{4{x}^{2}-x+5}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(4{x}^{2}-x+5),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-x=O(5)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(5)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(5)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nSince $5$ is just a constant multiple of $1,$ it follows by $\\text{the constant multiple property}$ that\n\n$$\nf=O(1)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$"}]}
